  "description": "Pick the right y-axis unit when creating or updating an insight via `posthog:insight-create` or `posthog:insight-update` — both TrendsQuery (`trendsFilter.aggregationAxisFormat`) and SQL insights (`DataVisualizationNode`, `chartSettings.yAxis[].settings.formatting`). Use when the agent is about to add a `formula` purely to convert units (e.g. dividing seconds by 60 to display minutes), when a `math_property` or SQL column is a duration, currency, ratio, or large count, or whenever the user mentions \"format the y-axis\", \"duration\", \"seconds\", \"minutes\", \"hours\", \"milliseconds\", \"ms\", \"percentage\", \"%%\", \"currency\", \"decimals\", \"axis label\", or \"axis unit\" in the context of a graph insight.",
